## Why This Is Asked

Tests integration of multimodal signals into ICA, a practical scenario in automotive settings where visual cues help resolve source ambiguity and nonstationary noise.

## Key Concepts

- Multimodal ICA with audio-visual priors
- Online whitening and natural-gradient demixing
- Cross-bin permutation tracking using AV alignment cues
- Latency constraints for real-time automotive use
- Evaluation including SDR, SIR, and lip-sync accuracy

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch for AV-regularized online ICA
let W = initialize(6,6);
for each frame t:
  X_t = frameAudio(mics, 32, 0.5);
  V_t = extractVisualFeatures(video);
  X_whitened = onlineWhiten(X_t);
  Y_t = W * X_whitened;
  W = naturalGradientUpdate(W, Y_t, V_t);
  permute = trackPermutationAV(Y_t, V_t);
  output = applyPermutation(Y_t, permute);
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design robust, real-time ICA in a manufacturing setting with nonstationary mixing and missing sensors, plus practical evaluation.

## Key Concepts

- Streaming ICA with convolutional mixing
- Frame-based whitening (ZCA)
- Online demixing with a 10×10 matrix
- Joint diagonalization vs per-bin ICA
- Handling missing channels via masking
- Forgetting factor for nonstationarity
- Latency and SDR/SIR evaluation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-update for online natural-gradient ICA (illustrative)
function updateDemixer(W, x, learningRate) {
  const y = W * x;
  const phi = Math.tanh(y);
  const grad = (1 - y * y) * x.transpose();
  W += learningRate * (I - phi * phi.transpose()) * grad;
  return W;
}
```

